"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nIt seems to pose a fundamental question about what  is to us living in an age of inability to empathize.  \nIt sharply points out the appearance of modern society that has become insensitive to the sadness of others.  \n\nLooking at the final scene of this book, it concludes with sudden, nonsensical miracles.  \nSo I think this book ultimately ended as a sad ending, leaving behind a fantasy containing the protagonist's hope.  "